+/* ═════════════ Nav under the promo bar (pure CSS, no JS offset) ═════════════
+   The design's nav is `position: fixed; top: 0` (home.css / every page.css —
+   generated). The promo strip (PromoBar, SSR) and the trial-sale bar sit IN
+   FLOW above the page, so at scroll 0 a fixed nav painted over them and only
+   snapped underneath once a hydrated script wrote `nav.style.top` (visible
+   overlap + a jump on first scroll, and PageRuntime/HomeScript ran
+   getBoundingClientRect on every scroll frame to keep doing it).
+   Fix: make the nav `position: sticky; top: 0` as the first child of the page
+   wrapper. It then sits exactly below whatever is above the wrapper (any
+   promo/sandbox height, wrapped to two lines on a phone, or dismissed), sticks
+   to the viewport top once that has scrolled away, and the SSR markup is
+   already correct: no hydration dependence, no layout shift. The negative
+   bottom margin gives the hero back the nav's own height (68px row + 1px
+   border) so the page lays out exactly as it did with a fixed nav.
+   While the mobile menu is open the nav is pinned fixed to the viewport so the
+   full-screen sheet (inset from the nav's height) lines up whatever scroll
+   offset the visitor is at; the overlay covers the promo bar for that moment. */
+.nxm :is(.nxm-home, .nxm-p) .nv {
+  position: sticky; top: 0; left: auto; right: auto;
+  margin-bottom: calc(-1 * (var(--nav-h, 68px) + 1px));
+}
+.nxm .nxm-nav-slot { display: contents; }
+.nxm :is(.nxm-home, .nxm-p) .nv.open { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; }
+/* The design gives `.nv.open` a backdrop-filter, which turns the nav into the
+   containing block of its own `position: fixed` mobile sheet — the sheet then
+   collapsed to a ~190px strip over the nav row (broken since launch, measured
+   at 390px). Opaque instead, so the sheet is positioned against the viewport. */
+.nxm :is(.nxm-home, .nxm-p) .nv.open { -webkit-backdrop-filter: none; backdrop-filter: none; background: #060913; }
+
 /* Trial-sale bar (components/marketing/PromoTrialPopup) on the new site: in
    normal flow at the very top instead of sticky 72px down (that offset was
-   tuned for the old site's header and made it overlap the new fixed nav,
-   owner 2026-09-27). The nav already positions itself under whatever is in
-   flow above the page (PageRuntime / HomeScript), and the bar scrolls away. */
+   tuned for the old site's header and made it overlap the new nav, owner
+   2026-09-27). The sticky nav above sits under whatever is in flow, and the
+   bar scrolls away. */
 .nxm .marketing-promo-stack .promo-bar { position: relative; top: auto; z-index: 1; }
